<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Krosno Odrzańskie</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Crossen an der Oder</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Krosno Odrzańskie, in German Crossen an der Oder, is a town in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> at the confluence of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bobr">Bóbr</a> and the Oder. A Silesian ducal town in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a>, it passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a> in the late 15th century and later formed part of the lands of Margrave John of Brandenburg-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kostrzyn-nad-odra">Küstrin</a>. It became Polish in 1945.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/krosno-odrzanskie.jpg" alt="Krosno Odrzańskie" width="320" height="234" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gorofil · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Krosno_Odrza%C5%84skie_-_Fara_Maryjna_1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
